      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct. The first portion of the function (L375-385) is duplicated from the first part of `memfd_create()`. My rationale for that is that since this is now available to the rest of the kernel, the arguments should be validated. This part could definitely be factored out into a helper.\n\nThe second portion of the function is similar to `memfd_create()`, but with the caveat that the given string is in the kernel\u0027s address space and not a userspace address. I wasn\u0027t sure how to factor that out without dropping the __user annotation from the name pointer. I could have two helpers that use some common knowledge:\n\n```\n/* Handles allocating the final name buffer and formatting the name */\nstatic char *memfd_create_name(char *name)\n\n/* Handles copying the name from userspace into a local buffer and calls memfd_create_name() */\nstatic char *memfd_create_name_user(const char __user *uname);\n```\n\nI wasn\u0027t sure if this was too clunky though.",
